{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"shared_outline\": {\n    \"shared_scope\": \"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\",\n    \"shared_argument\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\n    \"chapter_sequence\": [\"Ch1\", \"Ch2\", \"Ch3\", \"Ch4\", \"Ch5\", \"Ch6\", \"Ch7\"]\n  },\n  \"chapters\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch1\",\n      \"title\": \"实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"专注于人类观察性队列研究（回顾性与前瞻性），系统梳理不同实体瘤类型中微生物特征（分类学、功能、动态变化）与 ICI 临床结局的观察性关联。明确证据强度及肿瘤特异性，区分基线特征与治疗期间动态变化。纳入阴性或矛盾结果以平衡证据。不包含干预性试验数据（归入 Ch5）或纯机制解析（归入 Ch2/Ch3）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch2\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物调节 ICI 疗效的免疫学机制\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"阐述微生物通过调节宿主免疫细胞（DC、T 细胞、髓系细胞）及信号通路（STING、TLR 等）影响抗肿瘤免疫的具体生物学路径。重点区分动物模型因果证据与人类验证数据。侧重于细胞互作、受体信号及免疫细胞亚群平衡，不深入具体代谢物化学结构及浓度分析（归入 Ch3）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch3\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"深入分析关键微生物代谢物（SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸等）在调节 ICI 疗效中的作用，区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度数据，阐明分子靶点及作用机制。明确标注人体 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度数据的缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据），使用血浆数据作为系统性暴露的代理。不重复 Ch2 的免疫细胞互作细节，侧重于代谢物本身的化学性质、浓度及直接靶点。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch4\",\n      \"title\": \"外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"评估抗生素、PPIs、饮食等外部因素如何通过改变微生物组进而影响 ICI 疗效，特别是时间窗口和药物类别的特异性。基于观察性研究和系统综述。侧重于临床流行病学证据及生物学合理性解释，不包含方法学标准化讨论（归入 Ch7）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch5\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"总结 FMT、益生菌等干预措施在克服 ICI 耐药中的临床试验结果（包括阳性和阴性），分析供体选择、安全性及疗效持久性，明确证据等级。专注于干预性试验数据（I/II 期 vs III 期），不包含观察性关联数据（归入 Ch1）。明确标注无 Phase III RCT 证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch6\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"探讨微生物组与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的关联，分析疗效与毒性之间的权衡关系及预测标志物。特别关注供体特征与毒性的情境依赖性（如 FMT-LUMINate 中 Prevotella 与心肌炎）。侧重于毒性机制、预测及安全性管理，不重复 Ch5 的疗效数据，但需关联疗效 - 毒性权衡。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch7\",\n      \"title\": \"方法学挑战与未来研究方向\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"批判性评估当前研究的异质性来源（测序技术、队列差异），指出因果推断的局限及未来标准化研究的需求，明确未满足的证据缺口。基于方法学综述及前述章节中识别的证据缺口。不包含具体临床疗效数据复述（属 Ch1/Ch5），聚焦于方法论批判与路径规划。\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"supplement_requests\": [\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n      \"question\": \"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\n      \"status\": \"confirmed_missing\",\n      \"reason\": \"现有材料（P0582）明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在人类肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅提供了血浆数据。需确认是否有更新研究填补此缺口，若无，则需在综述中明确标注此为未满足的证据需求。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"phase_iii_rct_evidence\",\n      \"question\": \"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\n      \"status\": \"confirmed_missing\",\n      \"reason\": \"现有数据主要为 I/II 期试验（FMT-LUMINate, MITRIC, MIMic, TACITO）。TACITO 为 Phase 2a RCT，数值改善但统计显著性未报告。无已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT。需在综述中明确标注证据等级上限。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch5\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"jco2007_microbiome_data\",\n      \"question\": \"JCOG2007 III 期试验中肠道微生物组与 NSCLC 患者 ICI 疗效及毒性的具体关联数据是什么？\",\n      \"status\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"reason\": \"JCOG2007 III 期试验的附属微生物组分析数据未能获取（directed_read_not_admitted），需依赖其他 III 期生物标志物分析或注明证据缺口。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch1\", \"Ch4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"antibiotic_timing_meta\",\n      \"question\": \"抗生素暴露时机（治疗前 vs. 治疗后）对 ICI 疗效影响的系统 meta 分析证据是什么？\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"reason\": \"特定 meta 分析未能获取（AdmissionError），需依赖现有系统综述或回顾性队列数据。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch4\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"directed_reads\": [\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"reason\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch5\", \"Ch6\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0578\",\n      \"reason\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch5\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0582\",\n      \"reason\": \"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0585\",\n      \"reason\": \"JCOG2007 III 期试验的附属微生物组分析，需确认其具体的统计校正方法及亚组数据，以评估高级别证据强度。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch1\", \"Ch4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0478\",\n      \"reason\": \"跨队列黑色素瘤研究，需详细提取其关于‘无通用标志物’的具体统计依据及队列间异质性来源分析。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch1\", \"Ch7\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"handle\": \"P0327\",\n      \"reason\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\"Ch1\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"harmonization_notes\": [\n    \"章节边界协调：Ch1 专注于观察性人类数据，Ch5 专注于干预性试验数据，避免将 FMT 试验结果混入 Ch1 的关联证据中。Ch2 侧重于免疫细胞与信号通路机制，Ch3 侧重于具体代谢物分子及其浓度/靶点，避免机制章节内容重复。Ch6 专注于毒性机制与预测，虽引用 Ch5 试验数据，但分析重点为安全性与疗效 - 毒性权衡。\",\n    \"证据等级处理：所有章节需严格区分观察性关联与因果机制。Ch3 需明确标注人体 TME 肌苷浓度数据缺失，仅使用血浆数据作为代理。Ch5 需明确标注无 Phase III RCT 证据，避免过度宣称临床转化成熟度。\",\n    \"来源继承：除非在 excluded_source_handles 中明确列出，否则各章提案中的 source_handles 均继承至协调后的章节来源列表中。不重抄来源清单，由本地程序管理。\",\n    \"缺口处理：补充检索未找到匹配研究（如 TME 肌苷浓度、Phase III RCT）不等于该研究不存在，也不等于整个领域缺乏相关研究。未被满足的需求仅约束本次可写的结论范围，不得升级为领域层面的缺失判断。需在 Ch3 和 Ch5 中如实报告现有材料支持的范围。\",\n    \"矛盾解决：Ch1 中纳入阴性结果（如 P0327）以平衡阳性发现。Ch5 中并列呈现 FMT 阳性（FMT-LUMINate）与阴性（MITRIC）结果，避免发表偏倚。Ch4 中保留抗生素影响在不同癌种（如 HCC）中的异质性证据。\",\n    \"术语统一：统一使用‘免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）’、‘免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）’、‘肿瘤微环境（TME）’等术语。区分‘肠道微生物组’与‘肿瘤内微生物组’。\",\n    \"过渡逻辑：Ch1 现象 -> Ch2/Ch3 机制 -> Ch4 干扰因素 -> Ch5 干预策略 -> Ch6 安全性 -> Ch7 方法学与未来。确保各章之间有明确的逻辑衔接，如 Ch4 的外部干扰为 Ch5 的主动干预提供逻辑基础，Ch5 的干预结果为 Ch6 的毒性讨论提供实证。\"\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Request:**\n    *   **Role:** Academic Review Planning Editor (学术综述规划编辑).\n    *   **Goal:** Harmonize chapter proposals into a shared scope, ordered outline, chapter boundaries, concepts, terminology, and transitions for a long-form review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\n    *   **Input:** `harmonize_scope` task data containing `topic_id`, `research_question`, `shared_level1_outline` (scope, outline, argument, source selection principles, unresolved limits), and `chapter_proposals` (7 chapters with detailed threads, sources, exclusions, directed reads, etc.).\n    *   **Constraints:**\n        *   Return JSON only.\n        *   Do not write the actual review content (intro, abstract, conclusion are handled elsewhere).\n        *   Do not create an \"intro/overview\" chapter for planning purposes (planning info belongs in shared scope/outline, not a chapter).\n        *   Preserve source assignments (source_handles) unless explicitly excluded.\n        *   Merge/deduplicate supplement gaps and directed reads.\n        *   Resolve contradictions/overlaps between chapter proposals.\n        *   Ensure each chapter has a clear knowledge question/analysis task.\n        *   Maintain evidence hierarchy (observational vs. causal, animal vs. human, Phase I/II vs. III).\n        *   Respect unresolved limits (e.g., lack of human TME inosine concentration data, lack of Phase III RCTs).\n        *   Use Chinese for planning content (titles, purposes, etc.), keep paper titles/special names in original language.\n        *   Do not copy-paste source lists into the output (local program handles inheritance), only output necessary specific citations, exclusions, and structural adjustments.\n        *   Output structure: `shared_outline`, `chapters` (with `chapter_id`, `coordinated_scope`), `supplement_requests`, `directed_reads`, `harmonization_notes`.\n\n2.  **Review Input Data:**\n    *   **Shared Scope:** Solid tumors (Melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, CRC, etc.), ICIs (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4), Gut Microbiome (not intratumoral unless for mechanism contrast), Efficacy (ORR, PFS, OS) & Toxicity (irAEs), External factors (Abx, PPI, Diet), Interventions (FMT, Probiotics). Exclude hematological malignancies.\n    *   **Outline:** 7 Chapters (Ch1: Clinical Association, Ch2: Immune Mechanisms, Ch3: Metabolites, Ch4: External Factors, Ch5: Interventions, Ch6: Toxicity, Ch7: Methods/Future).\n    *   **Chapter Proposals:** Detailed threads, sources, exclusions, directed reads provided for each chapter.\n    *   **Conflicts/Overlaps:**\n        *   Ch1 (Clinical Association) vs. Ch5 (Interventions): Ch1 focuses on observational associations (cohorts), Ch5 on interventional trials (FMT, probiotics). Need to ensure clear boundary (Observation vs. Intervention).\n        *   Ch2 (Immune Mechanisms) vs. Ch3 (Metabolites): Ch2 focuses on cells/pathways (DC, T cells, TLR/STING), Ch3 on specific molecules (SCFAs, Inosine, Bile Acids). Some overlap exists (metabolites affect immune cells). Need to coordinate: Ch2 = Cell/Receptor/Signaling axis; Ch3 = Specific metabolite identity/concentration/mechanism.\n        *   Ch6 (Toxicity) vs. Ch1/Ch5: Toxicity is often reported alongside efficacy in Ch1/Ch5 studies. Ch6 should focus specifically on the *mechanism* and *prediction* of toxicity, and the efficacy-toxicity trade-off, rather than just reporting toxicity rates (which belongs in Ch1/Ch5 trial descriptions).\n        *   Ch4 (External Factors) vs. Ch7 (Methods): Ch4 discusses Abx/PPI/Diet as biological modifiers. Ch7 discusses methodological challenges (sequencing, confounding). Need to ensure Ch4 focuses on the *biological/clinical impact* of these factors, while Ch7 focuses on the *research methodology* challenges they pose.\n        *   Source Allocation: Many sources are assigned to multiple chapters (e.g., reviews covering multiple aspects). This is acceptable as long as the *use* is distinct (e.g., P0583 used in Ch5 for efficacy data, Ch6 for toxicity mechanism).\n        *   Directed Reads/Supplements: Several directed reads failed or were partial (e.g., Inosine TME concentration, Phase III RCTs). These need to be preserved as unresolved gaps in the final plan.\n\n3.  **Harmonization Strategy:**\n    *   **Shared Scope:** Refine to explicitly state the distinction between gut vs. intratumoral microbiome, and observational vs. interventional evidence.\n    *   **Chapter Boundaries:**\n        *   Ch1: Observational human data (cohorts, biomarkers).\n        *   Ch2: Immunological mechanisms (Cells, Receptors, Pathways) - primarily preclinical + human validation.\n        *   Ch3: Metabolite mechanisms (Specific molecules, concentrations, targets) - primarily preclinical + human plasma (note TME gap).\n        *   Ch4: Modifiers (Abx, PPI, Diet) - Clinical impact & biological plausibility.\n        *   Ch5: Interventions (FMT, Probiotics, LBPs) - Clinical trial data (Phase I/II vs III gap).\n        *   Ch6: Toxicity (irAEs) - Association, Mechanism, Efficacy-Toxicity coupling.\n        *   Ch7: Methods & Future - Standardization, Causality, Trial Design.\n    *   **Source Management:** Inherit all assigned sources from proposals unless explicitly excluded in the harmonization notes. Merge directed reads/supplements.\n    *   **Gaps:** Explicitly list the unresolved limits (Inosine TME concentration, Phase III RCTs, JCOG2007 data) in `supplement_requests` or `harmonization_notes` to ensure they are addressed as limitations in the writing phase, not as facts.\n    *   **Transitions:** Define logical flow between chapters (e.g., Ch1 Observation -> Ch2/Ch3 Mechanism -> Ch4 Modifiers -> Ch5 Intervention -> Ch6 Safety -> Ch7 Future).\n\n4.  **Drafting the JSON:**\n    *   `shared_outline`: Update based on harmonized scope.\n    *   `chapters`: Define `chapter_id`, `title`, `coordinated_scope` (specific focus to avoid overlap).\n    *   `supplement_requests`: Consolidate unresolved gaps from the input (Inosine, Phase III, JCOG2007, Abx timing meta-analysis).\n    *   `directed_reads`: Consolidate specific papers needing deep dive (P0583, P0578, P0582, etc.).\n    *   `harmonization_notes`: Explain how overlaps were resolved (e.g., Ch2 vs Ch3, Ch1 vs Ch5).\n\n5.  **Refining Constraints:**\n    *   *No source lists in output:* The prompt says \"不要在输出中重抄各章 source_handles/source_ids 清单\". I will omit the long lists of P-codes in the chapter objects and only mention specific key citations if necessary for clarification, or rely on the `harmonization_notes` to explain source inheritance. *Correction*: The prompt says \"only output necessary specific research citations, explicit exclusions and structural adjustments\". I will not list all P-codes.\n    *   *Chinese Language:* All planning text must be in Chinese.\n    *   *No Intro/Conclusion Chapters:* Ensure Ch1-Ch7 are substantive.\n    *   *Evidence Limits:* Ensure the lack of Phase III and TME inosine data is noted as a limit, not a fact.\n\n6.  **Final Check:**\n    *   Did I resolve the Ch2/Ch3 overlap? Yes, Cell/Pathway vs. Molecule/Concentration.\n    *   Did I resolve the Ch1/Ch5 overlap? Yes, Observational vs. Interventional.\n    *   Did I preserve the unresolved limits? Yes, in supplement_requests/notes.\n    *   Is the JSON structure correct? Yes.\n\n7.  **Constructing the Output:** (Mental Draft)\n    *   `shared_outline`: Keep the 7 chapters, refine titles/scopes.\n    *   `chapters`: Add `coordinated_scope` to each.\n    *   `supplement_requests`: List the failed/unfinished searches (Inosine TME, Phase III, etc.).\n    *   `directed_reads`: List the key papers identified for deep reading (P0583, P0578, P0582, etc.).\n    *   `harmonization_notes`: Explain the logic.\n\n    *Self-Correction on Source Lists:* The prompt says \"Don't copy the source_handles/source_ids list... only output necessary specific research citations...\". I will exclude the massive lists of P-codes from the chapter objects to save space and adhere to the instruction, focusing on the structural harmonization. I will reference specific key papers in `directed_reads` or `harmonization_notes` where critical.\n\n    *Self-Correction on Supplement Requests:* The input shows several `supplement_results` with status `unjudgeable` or `failed`. I need to carry these forward as `supplement_requests` in the harmonized plan so the writing phase knows these are gaps.\n\n    *Self-Correction on Directed Reads:* Several directed reads were `partial` or `failed`. I need to ensure the key ones (P0583, P0578, P0582) are listed as `directed_reads` for the writing phase to utilize the available material correctly.\n\n    *Final Plan:*\n    1.  Define `shared_outline` (Scope + 7 Chapters).\n    2.  Define `chapters` (ID, Title, Coordinated Scope).\n    3.  Define `supplement_requests` (The unresolved gaps).\n    4.  Define `directed_reads` (Key papers to consult).\n    5.  Define `harmonization_notes` (Resolution of overlaps, source inheritance, limit handling).\n\n    *Wait, one constraint:* \"Return JSON only.\" \"Don't copy source lists... only output necessary specific research citations...\". I will follow this strictly.\n\n    *Another constraint:* \"Preserve valuable level-1 tool results and do not reacquire review-reported original full texts.\" -> I should not request new searches for things we already have material for (like P0583 content), but I should list the unresolved gaps (Inosine TME) as requests that *failed* or need to be acknowledged as limits. The `supplement_requests` in the output should reflect what is *still needed* or *confirmed missing*. Since the tool results show \"unjudgeable\" or \"failed\" for Inosine TME and Phase III, I will list them as confirmed gaps to be stated in the review, not as new search tasks (unless I want to try again, but the prompt says \"preserve valuable level-1 tool results\"). I will list them as `supplement_requests` with status `confirmed_missing` to guide the writing.\n\n    *Actually, looking at the `harmonize_scope` task definition:* It asks to \"Merge and deduplicate supplement gaps and directed-read tasks... Preserve valuable level-1 tool results\". So I should list the gaps that remain open.\n\n    *Let's build the JSON.*","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":214301,"completion_tokens":5333,"total_tokens":219634,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2576,"text_tokens":5333},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":214301}},"created":1791138734,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-39713462-0687-9b8c-8a4d-83050e519658"}